            <ArticleTitle>Setting up a heart emergency centre.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>794-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the setting up of a 'heart emergency centre' linked to a pre-existing coronary care unit. The 'heart emergency centre' offers a new and efficient way of providing a fast and effective system for the assessment and management of patients with cardiac emergencies. This set-up can result in significant improvements in 'door to needle' time for thrombolysis, which has been shown to be beneficial both in terms of morbidity and mortality following myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
